
Changes since BlitzList V0.1
----------------------------

V1.0 - Alpha
------------
Finally managed to fix the list library which BlitzList used so heavilly so I
could carry on with this program. Six months to fix a library is a stupidly
long time. I'm getting slack :)

Had to make some major changes to the keyfile system for reasons best known 
only to myself. Old keys which were used by beta testers and myself are now
invalid I'm afraid.

Fixed a bug in the default archive command with the wrong syntax.

Finally sorted out the amigaguide generation so formatted output worked
properly.

Fixed up the flo file creation routines for auto generating file request files
by clicking on the filename.

Added in a new SystemAddress configuration option which is NOT optional. You
have to add this to old configuration files or Blitzlist will not work. It will
tell you if you don't have this setting correct. Format is 2.250.194.0

Corrected the amigaguide output to put file descriptions next to the filename.
Text versions stay as is because most text readers won't scroll left/right.

Made some considerable changes to the configuration test routines console 
output to include the system address check and tidy up the formatting. Looks
much neater again now.

Fixed up some real nasty bugs in the generating lists routines. Surprised it
worked at all. I'll leave debug code in for now just to be on the safe side as
blitzlist isn't too inteligent if configurations aren't set up properly yet.

Compiled new version without leaving my test flag in place this time ;)
Earlier versions had a flag set in the source code to reference directories
on my system if blitzlist was called with no arguments. This meant the 
default path mentioned in the Args didn't get referenced but mine did. Oops.

Removed the ViewKey option (no need for it). Also took out the list argument
as config lists directories anyway.

V1.0 - Beta
-----------
Added keyfile check routines and changes to program output text to use details.

Fixed a bug where it wouldn't report a problem if the config file could not
be found. <sheesh, how did I miss that?>

Added another option for VIEWKEY which can be used to pop up a requester showing
the keyfile details.

Did a lot of tidying up of the diz extraction code and added it to the output
guide files as well.

Put in restriction routines for unregistered use. This is the bit you'll all
hate me for :-)

  Now won't allow more than 25 directories in one config file.
  Won't let you use file_id.diz extraction.
  Won't let you use the AfterList command.
  Ansi output is disabled.
  Forced delays are present when generating lists.

Fixed bug where the delay in unregistered happened even if a valid key was
found. Silly sod forgot to share a variable :-)

Passed to Mike Handley for external testing.

V0.9d
-----
Found the ansi bug wasn't down to the fileid.diz additions causing a conflict
after all and fixed it properly this time :)

Added support for archive recognition and fixed blitzlist to use lha as well
as lzx for file_id.diz extraction.

Fixed nasty console output error text from archiver when a file_id.diz could
not be extracted.

Did some reformatting code in the diz extraction routines to tidy up output
list files.

Started work on the registration restriction routines.

V0.9c
-----
Found another bug in the ansi flags due to changed variable names.

Implemented crude File_ID.diz extraction routine for use as the file comments.
At the moment it only pulls them out if it's an lzx archive, only uses them for
the text lists, and the format routine needs a bit of work. End routine will
scan the extension suffix of the filename to enable recognition of lha files
as well. Guide implementation will be easy enough once I've debugged the text
handling routines.

V0.9b
-----

Fixed up the scan routines for generating guides so it wouldn't scan all files
in a directory once it confirmed that newfiles existed so that the listing
speed is significantly increased again, when generating newfile lists.

Fixed horrible bugs which generated multiple buttons for the same areas due
to sloppy work on my part. Took ages sussing this one :)

New option considered for BBSADVERT, where you could configure a text file
which would be automatically added to all archived lists, and could be a bbs
advert or similar.

Added config option for FILEIDDIZ recognition in program. Not sure if I'll add
it into the final release version, but just in case :-)

Newfiles lists now show number of days the file has been on the system based
on the dos datestamp.

More tidying up of the console output.

V0.9a
-----
NewList routine now works properly creating proper guide documents.

Fixed some small bugs with the archiving routines and passed arguments.

V0.9
----

Added routine to scan number of directory lines within config before actually
reading it in, so that the number of directorys configured in the program
can now be unlimited according to available memory etc.

Implemented the changes for all config options and reworked the scan routine
to make it truly asynchronous.

Redid the console output information again for more tidying up and put in the
extra info for new options in debug mode where it displays config information.

Managed to get under 50k executable when compiling without debugging handler
code.

Fixed some nasty bugs with the closing off of all files due to the new bits
that do all lists at once. Fixed a config reading error that didn't get the
path to the guide file correctly sometimes. Fixed a problem with empty
guide files generated and not passing the right arguments configured to the
archiver. Managed to make sure BlankGuide and BlankText are two different
config options which somehow slipped past me last time when I put the code
in.

Put in multiple header & footer support at last.

V0.8
----
BlitzList's newfiles function now works totally. I've not found any bugs
since spending 4 hours coding the bitch :\

Added extra lines available in header and footer files, as well as making
BlitzList use different ones for each list if required.

Added configuration for BlankLines in different lists rather than global.

Added configuration so that any generated file can be passed to afterlist
command wether it's an archive or not etc.

Implemented configurable filenames for .guide,.txt and newfiles lists. Much
more logical than generating each of them from a savepath config line. Ugh!

Reworked through all the seperate creation routines for each different output
file and put them within one routine so BlitzList doesn't do the same job
three times for each seperate list. Naturally this means it's 3 times as fast.
Roughly :)

V0.7
----
Fixed a minor bug in the example spot arexx script that caused an error on
exit with the quit routine.

Very Basic listing of newfiles now works. It's only available in ansi/text
mode for the moment. I'm re-working all the code so that I can make it both
faster, and work more efficiently in cases where guide,text and new output
lists all need to be generated, and it will do them asynchronously.

I'm working out a decent configuration structure which allows more flexibility
in how BlitzList works, and update the program to use the new format. This will
mean the last lot of major config changes, honest :)

Internal version. Not released!

V0.6
----
For once no configuration changes are needed :-)

Fixed a bug in the archive configuration where it would ask for an archive
suffix, even if no archiver was configured. Stupid mistake not declaring a
variable :)

Implemented the AfterList command function. Now you can use this for anything
from deleting the file afterwards (although BlitzList can do this for you
anyway :) ) to running an arexx script passing the filename in whatever format,
that will post the list into a message area on your bbs, or add it to a flo
file. Anything is possible, which is why the function was added in :)

Wrote an Example script for use with AfterList that works with Spot. Details of
how to use it are in the script. This could be used for auto posting of a new
files on the BBS list, of which I'll do an example once I've implemented new
files into the main program.

Fixed bug where it wouldn't run AfterList command unless it was in archive mode,
& also fixed bug where it wouldn't pass the filename to throw at external
command. Turned out to be use of different variable names which is a bug that's
been hiding for ages :)

V0.5
----
Added check routines for these new configuration lines

NEWFILELIST <path and name of file - .txt and .guide will be auto added>
NUMBERDAYS  <number of days for new files listing>
BLANKLINE   <puts a newline between each entry>

Added routines to display new config entries in debug mode, cleaned up the
config check console output to make it look MUCH nicer now :)

Redid the entire configuration routine in the end to shorten the need for
so many lines. See example version for radical changes as blitzList is a lot
more inteligent now and will add .guide .txt extensions etc, for example, and
will also let you configure an archiver line instead of just lha/lzx for 
future expansion. A few of the uneeded lines have been removed now. Your
configuration files will need changing for certain now, so please check
them if you've been using BlitzList prior to this release version.

Added configuration options for AfterList command which will be executed once
the list is generated. Added sub config options for PassText,PassGuide and
PassArchive which specify what file will be passed to the command. See example
configs and documentation for using this feature properly.

Implemented some more error checking in key areas when specified banners don't
exist.

Did some changes with how the outputed text and ansi files are done. It looks
a bit neater now with nicer colour usage and more information.

Fixed up the Ansi header text for each area so it's always centered.

Put in the archiving routines. Now it will archive up the lists within the
program so the external script isn't really nescessary apart from for generating
multiple lists.

Added some more console output so that BlitzList will report what it's currently
doing such as archiving, creating a guide, creating new list etc.

Updated the documentation. BlitzList has been radically changed since the
last version. Strongly recommend you re-read the thing.

Took out the Zeus restriction stuff. There's no real need for this program to
be Zeus BBS specific, so now it won't be.

Due to how powerfull this program will eventually end up, and the amount
of work I'll be putting in at the end of it, the final version will be cross
compatible for any bbs system supporting dos file comments, and be shareware,
so beta's from now onwards will be restricted to 5 directories without a
valid keyfile. A gui configuration program is now planned.

V0.4
----
Fixed a potentialy troublesome return code result due to undeclared variable.

Doubled the maximum number of directorys allowed for now. I will make this
proportional at a later date.

Wrote the routines to create AmigaGuide filelists as well as the plain ascii
lists. These won't use the Ansi settings even if specified obviously. The
created documents work just fine with Multiview. These guide files don't
support the creation of .REQ file request packets as yet, as I've not sussed
how they're done to date :-)

Fixed another bug with the Ansi setting. Now it will generate ansi output
files when configured to do so.

Fixed up the intro text to squash a bug preventing compilation date from
appearing. Some other cosmetic work done.

Added a configuration check for SAVEGUIDE with the LIST option.

Updated the example filelist generating script which I use here. This script
will become redundant later on once more external bits are added into the
main program such as archive options and deletion of archived files etc.

V0.3
----
Fixed silly bug where output would still be in ansi format when there was no
ansi setting configured in the config file. Thanks to Sam Morgan for pointing
that one out.

Edited format output a touch so that it uses 79 chars of the dos file comment,
puts a space next to the filename and comment field so auto posting filelists
into a message doesn't reflow all over the place, and did some minor code
optimising stuff to get an even faster speed. Blisters now :)

The hatched archives of BlitzList are now in a directory system that will
allow you to extract them directly into the Zeus directory structure replacing
old versions. Don't do this if you don't have your system configured similar
to the Zeus original distribution. The one below is how most people will have
it set up, like me, and is how it's archived here.

IE: Zeus:
         Bin/BlitzList/BlitzList
         Docs/BlitzList/BlitzList.doc
         Docs/BlitzList/BlitzList.changes
         Config/BlitzList/#?
         file_id.diz

Updated the doc file so it's actually a doc rather than a quick note :)

V0.2
----
Now recognises if there is no default config file as well as none specified
so it won't give a false error report.

Fixed the arg string routine so that using list won't make it generate a list
of files anyway as well as displaying the directorys in configuration file.

Stopped the directory paths list in the config being read beyond 200 entries
for now. That's the maximum and the way it was written it would still have
tried to go beyond that if the lines were present. Anything over 200 lines of
directory paths in the config will now be ignored. Also fixed the setup which
originally only allowed 100 entries despite the previous doc saying 200 :)

Added code to get names for headerfile and footerfile in. These point to text
files which will be added at the front and back of the filelist generated. At
this time you can use up to 20 lines in each file. Error checks have been
set this time so no chance of a guru if you use more :-)

Added code for ArchiveType,ArchiveName and DeleteOriginal lines to be read in
the configuration file. Archivetype is lha or lzx for compressing lists, 
ArchiveName is the name of archived list, and DeleteOriginal will remove the
original file once it's compressed.

Put in some program identify strings at the end of the generated file list.

Removed the Ansi Arg on the command line. No need for it. Ansi will be off
unless you have ANSI YES in the configuration file.

Implemented a lot more error checking. I can't bomb the beast now, and believe
me I've tried :-)

Added another arg for cli use. BlitzList <configfile> CONFIG will output an
ascii list of the settings configured within so it can be checked before the
config is actually used, in a readable format.

V0.1
----
First beta release. Basic or what :-)

